# A merge-group CI job's wall-time budget is 20 minutes (helpers/job-budget.py, milestone 721 (each merge-group CI job has a 20-minute budget)).
# A job that must exceed it gets a line here, in the same diff that lets it grow:
#
#     <job> <minutes> <reason, in words>
#
# `check` reads the minutes as that job's budget, warns at 85% of it (§254 (a gate prints what each item cost)) and fails above it.
# `timeout-minutes` in ci.yml may then be at most the new budget plus five. A line with no reason is
# refused, and so is one that does not raise the budget above 20. No job has one today: on 2026-10-03
# the slowest, `cpu-matrix`, ran a 15.0 minute median and a 16.6 minute maximum. It reached 19.8 on
# 2026-10-06 and failed at 20.1 to 21.0 on slow runners, because each model's boot of the growing
# riscv64 suite went from 1.6 to 3.1 minutes; it was split into two `cpu-matrix-shard` jobs rather
# than given a line here (ci.yml, above that job, has the measurement).
